From: gts7l project
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: repeated handover at debug level

The gts7l SLPI firmware raises its smp2p "ready" and "handover" bits
again while sensors stream (seen in the smp2p_notify_in trace: slave-kernel
0x0 -> 0x6), about 5 times a second, without any fatal/watchdog event.
Each one logged "Handover signaled, but it already happened" at error
level: ~72 lines a minute, ~100k a day. The repeat is already ignored;
log it at debug level.

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 58d5b85e5..c9eb8b027 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		dev_dbg(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
